_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_

**Add explicit event unsubscription in `useMeeting` cleanup.**

The hook registers participant listeners (and `roomJoined`) but cleanup only calls `client.leave()`. In docs patterns, explicit `off(...)` keeps lifecycle handling deterministic and avoids stale handlers.


<details>
<summary>Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
 useEffect(() => {
   const client = new RealtimeKitClient({ authToken });
-  client.self.on('roomJoined', () => setJoined(true));
+  const onRoomJoined = () => setJoined(true);
+  client.self.on('roomJoined', onRoomJoined);
   const update = () => setParticipants(client.participants.joined.toArray());
   ['participantJoined', 'participantLeft'].forEach(e => client.participants.joined.on(e, update));
   setMeeting(client);
-  return () => { client.leave(); };
+  return () => {
+    client.self.off('roomJoined', onRoomJoined);
+    ['participantJoined', 'participantLeft'].forEach(e => client.participants.joined.off(e, update));
+    client.leave();
+  };
 }, [authToken]);
```
</details>

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.

In @.agents/services/hosting/cloudflare-platform-skill/realtimekit-patterns.md
around lines 85 - 88, The hook useMeeting registers participant listeners
(client.participants.joined.on for 'participantJoined'/'participantLeft' and
likely client.on('roomJoined') or similar) but its cleanup only calls
client.leave(); modify the cleanup to explicitly remove those handlers before
leaving: call the corresponding off/unsubscribe methods (e.g.,
client.participants.joined.off('participantJoined', update),
client.participants.joined.off('participantLeft', update), and
client.off('roomJoined', roomJoinedHandler) or the exact handler references
used) to ensure deterministic lifecycle teardown in useMeeting.
```

</details>

